.TH XIL\-GUI "1" "2026\-07\-29" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-gui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-gui
[-h] [--port PORT] [--host HOST] [--share] [--output FILE] [--verbose]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the xil\-pipeline web dashboard (Gradio). Opens a browser UI with nine tabs: Setup (initialize a workspace / select the active show), Project (edit project.json), Episodes (workspace overview with parse/stems/DAW/master status), Run Stage (launch pipeline stages with live log streaming; dry\-run on by default), Speakers, Cast Config and SFX Config (edit the respective JSON configs), Audio Preview (browse and play stems in the browser), and Timeline (interactive HTML timeline).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI\,PORT\/\fR
Port to listen on (default: 7860)

.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI\,HOST\/\fR
Host address to bind (default: 127.0.0.1)

.TP
\fB\-\-share\fR
Generate a public ngrok URL for partner access (open, no auth)

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Append a timestamped session activity log to FILE

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-v\fR
Log detailed activity for the Timeline audio\-properties dialog (SFX open/save requests) to stdout and logs/xil_YYYY\-MM\-DD.log

.SH COMMENTS
Requires the [gui] extra:
  pip install 'xil\-pipeline[gui]'

Partner sharing (temporary 72h public URL, open access, no auth —
share only with trusted collaborators):
  xil\-gui \-\-share

